record templartorrent.observation.complete-piece-status/14 : observation {
    title "Linux client is fuzzed and syncs payload only at resume checkpoints; remaining boundaries"
    state superseded
    statement """
        2026-10-24, Linux x86_64 Ubuntu 26.04.1, kernel 7.0.0-31-generic, i7-13700H, rustc 1.99.0 (fuzzing on nightly 1.101.0 2026-10-04), committed on master at 2461a87. Seven libFuzzer targets in fuzz/ cover every parser that tracker, peer, .torrent, pasted and session-file bytes reach, plus an engine session under adversarial peers. They found crashes in rbit's bencode, info-hash hex, metainfo length and wire-frame handling and in the client's announce chunk decoding and persisted-hex decoding. All are fixed and pinned by stable tests, and a final 600 s run of every target was clean. FileStore no longer syncs each piece; the resume checkpoint reads the verified set, then sync_all()s every handle, and that is the only data barrier. rbit's peer transport now sets TCP_NODELAY. The 32 MiB loopback scenario takes 58 to 83 ms, against 3.6 to 22 s before, and magnet to first verified piece about 0.6 ms. 184 workspace tests pass on tmpfs; with TMPDIR on btrfs 182 pass and 2 fail only on the activation socket's SUN_LEN limit. Unchanged from 9b0874f: upload-slot ranking, HTTPS via rustls 0.23.46 with aws_lc_rs and no ring, pipeline depth is the preference cap, not an RTT bound. Remaining boundaries: pieces written after the last checkpoint are rechecked and there is no per-block journal; no power-loss test of the batched barrier, only process-kill tests; file identity is not a content hash; webseed and UPnP unavailable; download order inside one file follows the seeded tie-break; the rbit fork, now including the fuzz fixes and nodelay, must be re-applied on any upstream upgrade; rbit DHT, PEX, holepunch and UDP tracker parsers are unfuzzed because the client does not reach them; Windows paste, a real window event loop and public-swarm throughput are untested. Preview tests were not re-run.
        """
    observed_at git:2461a870f26e9ed2c7d6945837b694aeea31b10b
    method command
    watches [ "crates/**", "integration/**", "vendor/**", "fuzz/**" ]
    supersedes [ @templartorrent.observation.complete-piece-status/13 ]
    verified_by [
