record templartorrent.observation.internet-download-stall/1 : observation {
    title "One Internet run stalled with 25 unchoking peers; not reproduced"
    state superseded
    scope [ path "crates/templartorrent-engine/**", path "integration/rbit-adapter/**" ]
    statement """
        2026-10-25, Internet run 2 of the Ubuntu ISO (perf-results/2026-10-25-internet/run2.log), IPv4 only, code before the rbit get_peers fix. Verified bytes rose from about 630 s to 33.7 MB at 701 s, then stayed there until the run was stopped at 821 s. 25 of 28 connected peers had us unchoked and the smoothed download rate decayed to 0. The harness did not yet print lease or payload state. Run 4 on the committed code completed 6.48 GB without a stall, and run 5 saw none in 180 s. The harness now prints leased pieces, requests in flight, peers we cannot request from, pickable pieces, payload reservations, hash failures and peer errors every 10 s, so a recurrence shows which bound held. Suspects not ruled out: MAX_ACTIVE_PIECES (64) filled by leases on peers that stopped answering for under LEASE_TIMEOUT (30 s) at a time; payload reservations near the 48 MiB budget (run 4 sat at 44 MB); requests a choking peer discarded, which PeerActor::on_choke does not clear.
        """
    observed_at git:e6350dab1f5090a8160cc69f3238475633da1e7a
    method observation
    watches [ "crates/templartorrent-engine/src/**", "integration/rbit-adapter/src/driver.rs" ]
}

